    description: "WHAT (MOVES IDS).\n- An untyped `$x` contributes its NAME to the hashed signature, so renaming it moves the id: 823 parameters in grpc `src/php`, 90 in koel.\n- `?T` and `T|null` hash two texts.\n- Property types, class-constant types and a typed constant's type are not hashed (would move every typed property).\n- A method or property with explicit `public` hashes differently from one with no modifier (class constants do not, by PR #2200's rule).\n\nWHAT (does not move ids).\n- Enum cases, closures and arrow functions are not symbols; promoted constructor parameters are not emitted as fields; anonymous-class members have bare names.\n- `readonly array $d` with no visibility misparses (tree-sitter-php 0.24.1).\n- Intersection, DNF and by-reference-return types were measured on a fixture only: no PHP tree on the machine uses them.\n\nFixing a part marked MOVES IDS changes hashed input, so it belongs to the next stable-id bump, with a measured churn figure in the spec's history row.\n\nFound during PR 2 of the stable-id plan (the v15 bump), 2026-11-16 (PR #2200). Detail: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026/pr2/STATUS.md."  # 2a04
    fields: {}  # 2a04
